  "description": "Proposed reinstatement of window openings to south and west elevations",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;Unless otherwise hereby approved, all new works in respect of all the works hereby approved (and any other incidental works to be carried out in this connection) shall match the existing building in respect of materials used, detailed execution and finished appearance.\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure a satisfactory external appearance and safeguard the significance of the De Beauvoir Conservation Area.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, the windows in the southern elevation&amp;nbsp;(as shown on drawing no. PR-202-B) shall be fitted with obscured glass to a minimum of Pilkington Level 3 (or equivalent). The windows shall be permanently retained as such thereafter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\nREASON: To ensure neighbouring amenity is protected.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
